.TH IMAP2PST 1 "2026" "imap2pst 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
imap2pst \- migrate an IMAP mailbox into a Microsoft Outlook PST file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imap2pst
.B \-\-host
.I HOST
.B \-\-user
.I USER
.B \-\-output
.I FILE.pst
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imap2pst
connects to an IMAP server, fetches every message in every folder, and writes a
Unicode PST file that Microsoft Outlook opens directly. It runs headless on
Linux and needs neither Outlook nor MAPI nor Windows.
.PP
Folder hierarchy, message bodies, attachments, embedded messages and non-ASCII
text are preserved. The PST is written as the migration runs, so memory stays
proportional to the number of messages rather than to the size of the mailbox.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Connection
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST"
IMAP server hostname. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " N"
Port. Defaults to 993 with TLS, 143 without.
.TP
.BI \-\-user " USER"
Login name. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-password " PASS"
Password. Visible in the process list; prefer
.BR \-\-password\-env .
.TP
.BI \-\-password\-env " VAR"
Read the password from the named environment variable.
.TP
.BI \-\-oauth2\-bearer " TOKEN"
Use an XOAUTH2 bearer token instead of a password. Untested against a real
provider.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tls
Plain IMAP, upgrading opportunistically when the server offers STARTTLS.
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Do not verify the server certificate.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " N"
Per-request timeout in seconds. Default 120.
.TP
.BI \-\-retries " N"
Attempts per request before giving up. Default 3.
.SS Selection and output
.TP
.BI \-\-output " FILE.pst"
Destination PST file. Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-folder " NAME"
Migrate only this folder. May be repeated.
.SS Throughput and restarts
.TP
.BI \-\-batch " N"
Messages per fetch round trip. Default 50.
.TP
.BI \-\-batch\-bytes " N"
Cap on the message source held in one batch. Default 32M.
.TP
.BI \-\-spool " DIR"
Keep fetched message source in this directory and reuse it on a later run, so
an interrupted migration does not download it again. The PST itself is always
rebuilt from scratch.
.TP
.BI \-\-progress " N"
Report progress every N messages. Default 100; 0 turns it off.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Print only the final summary.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Log progress and libcurl's own protocol trace.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every message was migrated.
.TP
.B 1
The run finished but some messages could not be fetched or parsed. They are
listed by folder and UID on standard error.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was wrong.
.SH EXAMPLES
Migrate a whole account, reading the password from the environment:
.PP
.nf
.RS
IMAP_PASSWORD=secret imap2pst \\
    \-\-host imap.example.com \\
    \-\-user alice@example.com \\
    \-\-password\-env IMAP_PASSWORD \\
    \-\-output alice.pst
.RE
.fi
.PP
Migrate one folder, keeping a spool so a second run is cheap:
.PP
.nf
.RS
imap2pst \-\-host imap.example.com \-\-user alice@example.com \\
    \-\-password\-env IMAP_PASSWORD \-\-folder INBOX \\
    \-\-spool /var/cache/imap2pst \-\-output inbox.pst
.RE
.fi
.SH SECURITY
.B \-\-password
puts the secret in the process list, where any user on the machine can read it.
Use
.B \-\-password\-env
instead. The spool directory holds message source in plain text; it is the
whole mailbox on disk, unencrypted, and should be treated accordingly.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imapsync (1)
.SH BUGS
The PST is written append-only: nothing is freed or reused, so the file is
larger than one Outlook would write. Calendar items, contacts and tasks
arriving over IMAP are stored as ordinary mail.
